# IDNE core rules

Read `AGENTS.md` and `OFFLINE_AI/CURRENT_STATE.md` before substantial work.

## Must do

- Prefer authoritative specs over chat memory (see `AGENTS.md` document priority).
- Preserve fixed world truth; do not weaken validators for PASS.
- Use staged Generator v2 (one layer at a time); never one-shot full adventures.
- Run focused tests, then `python -m unittest discover -s tests`.
- Label facts vs observations vs assumptions vs proposals.
- Update `OFFLINE_AI/SESSION_HANDOFF.md` after significant work.

## Must not do

- Modify engine, schemas, validators, or adventures unless the task explicitly requires it.
- Treat untrusted simulator metrics as adventure facts.
- Invent canonical IDs, schemas, or measured local-model settings.

## Reference files (do not duplicate here)

- `OFFLINE_AI/OPERATING_RULES.md` — workflow discipline
- `OFFLINE_AI/ARCHITECTURE_MAP.md` — system map
- `OFFLINE_AI/KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md` — current gaps
- `OFFLINE_AI/TASK_TEMPLATE.md` — scoped task format
- `IDNE_DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW.md` — lifecycle
- `ADVENTURE_GENERATOR_V2_SPEC.md` — generator norms
- `SIMULATOR_V2_SPEC.md` — simulator norms
